      en: "Ivanovskaya Gorka is a historic district in Moscow, located on a hill between Tverskaya Street and the Moscow River. It is one of the oldest neighborhoods in Moscow, featuring buildings from the 17th to 19th centuries. Originally a residential area for the nobility, it now houses embassies and museums. The area is known for its narrow lanes and old churches. Ivanovskaya Gorka has witnessed many historical events. It is named after the Church of St. John the Baptist. It is a popular tourist destination.",
